1. EXCLUSIVE OWNERSHIP AND RESERVATION OF RIGHTS
All rights, title, and interest in and to this software repository—including,
without limitation, all source code, software architecture, user interface
components, style sheets, scripts, structured datasets, historical archives,
editorial articles, photographs, portraits, downloadable PDF documents, audio
files, and graphic assets—are and shall remain the exclusive property of the
Associazione Italiana Arbitri - Sezione di Agrigento (and, where applicable,
the Associazione Italiana Arbitri [AIA] and the Federazione Italiana Giuoco
Calcio [FIGC]).

All rights not expressly granted in writing by the Rights Holder are strictly
reserved.

2. NO PUBLIC OR OPEN-SOURCE LICENSE GRANTED
Making this repository publicly visible for institutional transparency,
hosting deployment, and authorized technical maintenance does NOT constitute a
grant of any open-source, public domain, or implied license.

Without the prior, explicit written authorization of the Associazione Italiana
Arbitri - Sezione di Agrigento, it is strictly prohibited to:
  (a) copy, reproduce, duplicate, distribute, or publicly display any part of
      the source code, design system, datasets, texts, or media assets;
  (b) modify, adapt, translate, reverse-engineer, or create derivative works
      based upon this repository or any part thereof;
  (c) use the software, layout, or contents for any commercial, third-party, or
      unauthorized institutional purpose;
  (d) extract, scrape, index, or reuse personal data, member rosters, or
      photographs of referees, board members, presidents, or award recipients,
      which are additionally protected under Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR)
      and Italian Data Protection Law (Legislative Decree 196/2003 as amended).

3. INSTITUTIONAL EMBLEMS, TRADEMARKS, AND NAMES
The names, acronyms, crests, vector emblems, and official logos of the
"Associazione Italiana Arbitri" (AIA), "Federazione Italiana Giuoco Calcio"
(FIGC), "Associazione Italiana Arbitri - Sezione di Agrigento", and "Premio
Nazionale Giudice Beato Rosario Livatino" are protected institutional
designations and symbols. Nothing in this repository grants any right to use
such logos, marks, or designations.

4. AUTHORIZED CONTRIBUTIONS
Any individual who submits code, data, documentation, or assets to this
repository via Pull Request or other means acknowledges and agrees that all
accepted contributions are provided voluntarily and are irrevocably assigned to
the Associazione Italiana Arbitri - Sezione di Agrigento, becoming subject to
the exclusive ownership terms of this License.

